<div class="article-detail-page">
    <div class="article-body">

        <p>If your payment is declined on Lively, you can retry or update your payment method. Here's how to fix common problems with payment and what to know about unexpected charges.</p>
        <p>This article covers troubleshooting payments made directly through Lively. If you used Klarna or Affirm, check out <a asp-action="BuyNowPayLater">Buy Now, Pay Later</a>.</p>

        <p><strong>On this page:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#why-payments-decline">Why payments decline</a></li>
            <li><a href="#fix-declined-payment">Fix a declined payment</a></li>
            <li><a href="#troubleshoot-charges">Troubleshoot charges</a></li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="why-payments-decline">Why payments decline</h2>
        <p>Payments can fail for a few reasons:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Not enough funds available</li>
            <li>Card expired or not activated</li>
            <li>Incorrect card details (number, expiration date, CVV/security code, billing address)</li>
            <li>Billing address doesn't match your bank's records</li>
            <li>Bank flagged the payment for review</li>
        </ul>

        <p>If you've confirmed everything looks correct and your payment still won't go through, contact your bank to investigate the issue before you retry payment.</p>
        <p>In the meantime, you can try your purchase using a different payment method.</p>

        <h2 id="fix-declined-payment">Fix a declined payment</h2>
        <p><strong>During a live show</strong></p>
        <p>When you bid on a item and your payment declines, you'll get a notification in Lively asking you to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Add new payment method</strong> (use a different card or payment option), or</li>
            <li><strong>Retry payment</strong> (try the same method again)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Before retrying, make sure you've <a asp-action="FixPaymentIssue">fixed any issues</a> with your payment method.</p>

        <div class="text-center my-4">
            <img src="/help_centre_img/help_area/fixing_declined_payment.png" alt="Payment declined notification screen in Lively app"
                 class="img-fluid" style="border-radius: 12px;" />
        </div>

        <p>The seller is also notified and may ask you to fix your payment before the show ends.</p>

        <p><strong>If payment isn't fixed before the show ends:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>The order is automatically canceled</li>
            <li>You won't be charged</li>
            <li>The seller won't ship and can relist the item</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>At checkout outside a show</strong></p>
        <p>If your payment fails while purchasing outside a show:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>In the app, you'll see a message that your <strong>payment was declined</strong></li>
            <li>On web, you'll see a message that your <strong>order wasn't placed</strong></li>
        </ul>
        <p>You can then update your payment method, or retry the same method <a asp-action="FixPaymentIssue">once issues are resolved</a>.</p>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="troubleshoot-charges">Troubleshoot charges</h2>
        <h3>Why was I charged ₦10,000?</h3>
        <p>If you see an pending charge for ₦10,000, it's usually a temporary pre-authorization when you request to become a <a asp-action="BuyingOnLively">Verified Buyer</a>. This helps confirm that you have funds available and a valid payment method before making a purchase during a show.</p>
        <p>The hold won't fully process and should disappear from your bank statement within a few days.</p>

        <h3>Why am I seeing a recurring charge?</h3>
        <p>Lively doesn't offer subscriptions. If you see a recurring charge, it may be because:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>You used <a asp-action="BuyNowPayLater">Buy Now, Pay Later</a> (Klarna, Affirm), and it's part of your installment plan</li>
            <li>Your bank grouped multiple purchases or labeled them as a subscription</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If you're unsure, wait for the charges to fully process. If they don't add up, <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">contact our Support team</a> with a screenshot and we'll help investigate.</p>

        <h3>Why am I seeing duplicate charges?</h3>
        <p>Duplicate charges can appear if attempted payments fail. Failed charges usually drop off within a few days.</p>
        <p>If the duplicate charges don't disappear from your bank statement, <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">contact Support</a> with a screenshot and we'll help investigate.</p>

        <h3>Why am I seeing duplicate charges?</h3>
        <div class="article-info-box">
            Check your orders under <strong>Activity &gt; Purchases</strong> in Lively. If the order isn't listed, it wasn't successful.
        </div>
        <div class="article-info-box mt-3">
            Any charge you see on your bank statement is likely a temporary hold from a failed payment. Failed payments should disappear from your statement within a few business days.
        </div>

